<h1>Limits</h1>
<p class="lead">The edge build is the Soli interpreter and the request pipeline, without the
server around them. What needs a socket, a thread, a subprocess or a disk stays with
<code>soli serve</code>.</p>

<div class="grid two">
  <article>
    <h2>Runs on the edge</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Routes, controllers, <code>before_action</code>, middleware</li>
      <li>Views, layouts, partials, components, view helpers</li>
      <li>Query strings, URL-encoded and multipart forms, JSON bodies and responses</li>
      <li>I18n from <code>config/locales</code></li>
      <li>Models on <a href="/#sqlite">D1</a> (or a Durable Object per tenant), on
          <a href="/#postgres">Postgres through Hyperdrive</a> with transactions, or on SoliDB over HTTPS</li>
      <li>Attachments in <a href="/#r2">R2</a>, with <code>Range</code>, and
          <a href="/#images">image transforms</a> on read</li>
      <li>Background jobs through <a href="/#queues">Cloudflare Queues</a></li>
      <li><a href="/live">LiveView</a>, each instance's socket held by a Durable Object</li>
      <li><code>static cron</code> jobs, on Cloudflare Cron Triggers (<a href="/d1">/d1</a> shows an hourly one)</li>
      <li>The <code>HTTP</code> class, over the Worker's <code>fetch</code></li>
      <li>Static files from <code>public/</code>, served by Cloudflare</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Stays with soli serve</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Other WebSockets, server-sent events and streamed bodies (answered with a 501);
          LiveView <code>tick</code>, live queries and <code>live_update</code></li>
      <li><code>Cron.schedule</code> (a <code>static cron</code> runs on a Cron Trigger), SMTP (mailers send over HTTP),
          jobs delayed past 12 hours</li>
      <li>Resumable and direct uploads, files over about 20 MB, anything that writes files</li>
      <li>MySQL, SQLite files and the native SoliDB driver; transactions on D1</li>
      <li><code>--dev</code>: hot reload, the dev bar, the REPL</li>
      <li>PDF, Office documents, the <code>Image</code> class, subprocesses</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</div>

<h2>Worth knowing</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>One request at a time per isolate.</strong> A request suspended on a query keeps
      its isolate; Cloudflare spreads load over more isolates.</li>
  <li><strong>A Rust panic ends the isolate</strong>, where <code>soli serve</code> would answer
      a 500 and carry on. The next request boots a fresh one.</li>
  <li><strong>Size.</strong> About 11.7 MB of WebAssembly (3.6 MB gzipped). Workers limit the
      uncompressed bundle to 64 MiB on every plan, free included, and no longer cap the
      compressed size. The limit that still applies is startup time: 1 second. The Postgres
      driver adds about 40 KB.</li>
  <li><strong>Sessions.</strong> The in-memory store lives as long as an isolate; use the
      <code>cookie</code> driver with <code>SOLI_SESSION_SECRET</code>.</li>
</ul>
